        "original_id": "574f15fe-14bb-5150-bfbb-364b2ddd4e87",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: New Hampshire Northcoast Corporation, Pan Am Railways, Boston Sand & Gravel\n- Places: Dover, New Hampshire, Charlestown, Massachusetts, Mattawamkeag, Maine, Rotterdam Junction, New York\n- Concepts: rail interchange, Class II regional railroads, holding companies\n\nFacts:\n- Before March 2006, Pan Am Railways was known as Guilford Rail System.\n- Pan Am Railways is an American holding company that owns and operates Class II regional railroads.\n- Pan Am Railways' railroad network covers northern New England from Mattawamkeag, Maine, to Rotterdam Junction, New York.\n- New Hampshire Northcoast Corporation interchanges rail cars with Pan Am Railways in Dover, New Hampshire.\n- Pan Am Railways then takes those rail cars to the Boston Sand & Gravel plant in Charlestown, Massachusetts.",
